⚠️ Notes & troubleshooting
Voice: use Chrome/Edge on Android/desktop for continuous Speech-to-Text (Web Speech API). iOS Safari supports tap-to-talk; typing works everywhere. If the mic icon is hidden, your browser lacks SpeechRecognition — the type-a-command box does everything.
Transcripts: captions come from YouTube's public endpoints. A few videos have captions disabled by the creator, and VPN/datacenter networks can be blocked — run from your home Wi-Fi. (The server tries 4 fallback layers automatically.)
Trending: uses YouTube's trending feed when available, with an automatic viral-search fallback so it works from any network.
No API keys needed for anything except optional Gemini upgrades. Keep the server on your own machine/phone — it's private, nothing is stored in the cloud (timetable + settings live in localStorage).
Security: it's a local tool — don't expose it to the public internet without auth if you set a Gemini key.
